==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|ydropsy}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|idropsie}}, {{m|fro|ydropisie}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|hydropisis}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|ὕδρωψ|}}, from {{m|grc|ὕδωρ||water}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|dropsies}}

# {{label|en|pathology}} Swelling, [[edema]], often from chronic obstructive pulmonary disease [[COPD]].
#* '''1911''', ''Joseph Addison'', [[S:1911 Encyclopædia Britannica/Addison, Joseph|Encyclopædia Britannica]]:
#*: The disease under which Addison laboured appears to have been asthma. It became more violent after his retirement from office, and was now accompanied by '''dropsy'''.

